sidebar:"Sidebar",hc_label:"Hadith collection",hc_gen:"General library ({n})",hc_nw:"An-Nawawi's Forty ({n})",nw_title:"Imam an-Nawawi's Forty Hadith",nw_intro:"Imam Yahya ibn Sharaf an-Nawawi (d. 676 AH) gathered these 42 narrations as a foundation of the religion. They appear here in his own numbering, kept apart from the general library. Grades are as HadeethEnc gives them: Sahih and Hasan are marked separately, and a dot or label marks a grade that a scholar should review.",nw_prog:"{k} of {n} read",nw_jump:"Go to hadith",nw_no:"Hadith {n} of {t}",nw_mark:"Mark as read",nw_done:"Read",nw_sahih:"Sahih",nw_hasan:"Hasan",nw_flag:"Grade: needs review",nw_takhrij:"Takhrij (who recorded it)",nw_refs:"Collection numbers on sunnah.com",nw_refs_none:"sunnah.com links no collection number for this hadith; see the takhrij above.",nw_also:"Also in the general library",nw_review:"Numbers, Arabic, takhrij and grades were checked against sunnah.com and HadeethEnc.com on 18 October 2026. Not reviewed by a qualified scholar. Reading progress is saved on this device only.",up_title:"Fasting planner and upcoming dates",fp_list:"Your planned fasts",fp_none:"No fasts planned yet. Select a day and tick “I plan to fast this day”.",up_dates:"Upcoming Islamic dates",cd_until:"{p} begins in",cd_off:"Countdown unavailable: today's times could not be calculated reliably for this location.",
